            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.071,
            0.494,
            0.089
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.372,
            0.113,
            0.628,
            0.134
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter Summary"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.152,
            0.882,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "An equation of the form "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax + by + c = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , where a, b and c are real numbers, such that a and b are not both zero, is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "linear equation in two variables",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.214,
            0.879,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• A linear equation in two variables has infinitely many solutions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.239,
            0.881,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "An equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = m x + d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "slope-intercept form",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of a linear equation in two variables. Here ‘m’ represents the slope and ‘d’ the y-intercept. The line cuts the y-axis in the point (0, d)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.303,
            0.881,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Every point on the graph of a linear equation in two variables is a solution of the linear equation. Moreover, every solution of the linear equation is a point on the graph of the linear equation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.366,
            0.88,
            0.406
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A pair of linear equations in two variables can be represented, and solved, both algebraically and graphically."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.41,
            0.881,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• A pair of linear equations can be solved algebraically using the Method of Substitution or the Method of Elimination."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.454,
            0.881,
            0.495
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• If a pair of linear equations is given by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a_{1}x + b_{1}y + c_{1} = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a_{2}x + b_{2}y + c_{2} = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , then the following cases may arise:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.499,
            0.88,
            0.563
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { a _ { _ 1 } } { a _ { _ 2 } }   \\neq   \\frac { b _ { _ 1 } } { b _ { _ 2 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " : In this case, the pair of linear equations "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "has a unique solution",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.568,
            0.881,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "⸰ "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{a_{1}}{a_{2}}=\\frac{b_{1}}{b_{2}}\\neq\\frac{c_{1}}{c_{2}}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " : In this case, the pair of linear equations "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "does not have a solution",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.638,
            0.881,
            0.704
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "⸰ "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{a_{_1}}{a_{_2}}=\\frac{b_{_1}}{b_{_2}}=\\frac{c_{_1}}{c_{_2}}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " : In this case, the pair of linear equations "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "has infinitely many solutions",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.709,
            0.881,
            0.749
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• The graph of a pair of linear equations in two variables is represented by two lines."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.748,
            0.881,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "⸰ If the lines intersect at a point, then that point is the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "unique solution",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the two equations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.787,
            0.881,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If the lines coincide, then there are "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "infinitely many solutions",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", each point on the line being a solution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.825,
            0.881,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "⸰ If the lines are parallel, then the pair of equations has "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "no solution",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
